  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A string is called a **happy prefix** if is a **non-empty** prefix which is also a suffix (excluding itself).\n\nWith a string `s`, output *the **longest happy prefix** of* `s`. Output an empty string `\"\"` if no such prefix exists.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"level\"\nOutput: \"l\"\nExplanation: s contains 4 prefix excluding itself (\"l\", \"le\", \"lev\", \"leve\"), and suffix (\"l\", \"el\", \"vel\", \"evel\"). The largest prefix which is also suffix is given by \"l\".\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"ababab\"\nOutput: \"abab\"\nExplanation: \"abab\" is the largest prefix which is also suffix. They can overlap in the original string.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 105`\n* `s` includes only lowercase English letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
